id: banner-making-of
skill: social-media/blog-post
lang: th
voice: personal blog, first person ผม, ครับ only at the opening and sign-off
prompt_th: "ช่วยคิดหัวข้อของ Blogpost เกี่ยวกับ Banner ที่สร้างล่าสุดจาก Session นี้, โดยอยากจะบอกิธีว่าทำขึ้นมาได้ยังไง พร้อมขั้นตอน และวิธีการ ปิดท้ายด้วยว่า ถ้าอยาก ... หากสนใจ <hook คิดต่อ> จ้างผมได้เลยที่ fastwork"
prompt_en: "Help me come up with titles for a blog post about the banner made most recently in this session. I want to tell how it was made, with the steps and the method, and close with: if you want ..., if you're interested <a hook to continue>, hire me on Fastwork."
cta_url: "https://fastwork.com/user/th3r"
min_titles: 5
min_steps: 4
max_chars: 2000
method_terms[4]: banner.py,bench.py,.banner.json,github.com/th3r-dev/th3-skills
hook_terms[2]: ถ้าอยาก,หากสนใจ
facts[14]{id,text}:
  sources,"Rules came from three sources: AlphaGraphics, Adobe Express and the ui-ux-pro-max banner-design skill."
  layouts,"Layouts came from Dribbble searches and the Inspo archive; UI8 sits behind a Cloudflare bot check."
  size,"Fastwork shows service images in a 16:9 box, 840 x 473 on the page and 960 x 540 served, so the banner is 1920 x 1080."
  layers,"The four steps are the four layers of the GitHub README: Interface, Services, Data, Platform."
  spec,"The banner is a spec file, th3r.banner.json, rendered to SVG by banner.py."
  bench,"bench.py checks the safe zone, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, core text of at least 10px on a 400px-wide phone card, and a PNG under 1 MB."
  fail-edge,"Failure 1: with no logo, the 120px name sat inside the 96px edge band."
  fail-badge,"Failure 2: the Open for freelance badge came out 4.7px on a phone card; it moved to the support zone."
  fail-fact,"Failure 3: a facts row said Remote, which was never published; the author caught it while re-reading (the bench cannot know what is true) and replaced it with UTC+7 from the GitHub README."
  styles,"Three styles: blueprint, paper, flat; blueprint's lowest contrast is 8.74:1."
  variants,"Five layouts exist: columns, rail, stairs, bento, stack; the th3-skills preview has 12 variants and all pass."
  agent-built,"The banner was built with an AI agent, Claude Code: it wrote the spec and the renderer and ran every bench."
  skills-source,"The skills used (the design skill with banner.py and bench.py) come from th3-skills, the author's public repo: https://github.com/th3r-dev/th3-skills"
  agents,"A label along the request line says AI agents work on every layer: Claude Code + th3-skills."
rubric[9]{id,check}:
  titles,"at least min_titles title options in titles.md"
  steps,"at least min_steps numbered how-it-was-made steps in the post"
  method,"names every method_terms item"
  hook,"a hook_terms phrase appears after the steps and before the CTA link"
  cta,"links cta_url"
  dashes,"no em or en dashes in prose (humanizer)"
  facts,"every multi-digit or decimal number in the prose appears in facts"
  length,"the text a reader sees is at most max_chars characters (code, images, URLs and markdown marks not counted)"
  images,"a cover, an image in every step, and a closing image"
